Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.34 phase 1: equip from the Items menu

P6.34 phase 1 (docs/P6.34_MENU_FLOW.md). In the Items menu, Cross on a weapon,
armor or accessory (the options 2 to 4, whose lists also show worn-only items)
did nothing in the original game (patch 0180 logs it). With the key
items_equip_from_items on (default 1; DW3_ITEMS_EQUIP_FROM_ITEMS=0 or the file
key 0 gives the original behavior and the 0180 line back):

* STSTATUS_runItemList state 2 (item_list.c): Cross on an equipment item with a
  copy in the bag does what Cross on a usable item does (SOUND_SELECT, itemIndex
  and item set, STSTATUS_showItemHelp(-1), substate + 1), so the existing
  STSTATUS_leaveItemList opens the partner step. A worn-only item (the lists are
  built with the "all" flag, so GAME.items is 0) is refused with a log line.
* STSTATUS_chooseItemMember (item_screen.c): Cross on an equipment item calls
  portEquipCheck (slot from dw3_port_items_equip_slot, a pure function over the
  record kind; STSTATUS_canEquip for the partner mask and the hand) and, if it
  passes, the same fades as using an item, then portEquipApply, which calls
  STSTATUS_equip (the only writer of GAME.items, GAME.equippedItems and
  PartnerStats.equip), puts the result line in the help window (item and
  partner names from the game's own tables, the words from
  port/items_menu in the EU language) and enters the used-item substates
  (0x64, 0x65). A partner that cannot equip stays selectable: Cross is
  refused with SOUND_CURSOR, a log line and the "cannot equip" line, no state
  change. Moving the cursor restores the item's help. Triangle logs the
  cancel.
* STSTATUS_confirmItemUsed (item_screen.c): the list was already rebuilt there
  (ITEM_FUNCS.list); one log line says its count and where the item is, after
  an equip. The reopen path (STSTATUS_reopenItemList) creates the list again
  on the item, so a stack used up stays listed while worn.

Policy, logs and strings in port/items_menu/items_menu.c; the unit test is
tools/tests/items_menu_main.c.

